  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\alpha, \\beta$ be the roots of the equation $x^{2}-6 x-2=0$ with $\\alpha>\\beta$. If $a_{n}=\\alpha^{n}-\\beta^{n}$ for $n \\geq 1$, then the value of $\\frac{a_{10}-2 a_{8}}{2 a_{9}}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "3",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x^{2}-6 x-2=0$\r\n$x^{n}-6 x^{n-1}-2 x^{n-2}=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow x^{n}-2 x^{n-2}=6 x^{n-1}$\r\nfor $n=10$\r\n$x^{10}-2 x^{8}=6 x^{9}$\r\n$\\alpha^{10}-2 \\alpha^{8}=6 \\alpha^{9}$\r\n$\\beta^{10}-2 \\beta^{8}=6 \\beta^{9}$\r\n$\\left(\\alpha^{10}-\\beta^{10}\\right)-2\\left(\\alpha^{8}-\\beta^{8}\\right)=6\\left(\\alpha^{9}-\\beta^{9}\\right)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow a_{10}-2 a_{8}=6 a_{9}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{a_{10}-2 a_{8}}{2 a_{9}}=3$"
  }
